<h1>stooge sort</h1>
<p>
(algorithm)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
A terribly inefficient <a href="sort.html"><em>sort</em></a> algorithm that swaps the top and bottom items if needed, then (<a href="recursive.html"><em>recursively</em></a>) sorts the bottom two-thirds, then the top two-thirds, then the bottom two-thirds again.
</p>

<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="bozoSort.html"><em>bozo sort</em></a>, <a href="bogosort.html"><em>bogosort</em></a>, <a href="luckySort.html"><em>lucky sort</em></a>.
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>
<h2>Implementation</h2>
Pat Morin's <a href="https://cglab.ca/~morin/misc/sortalg/" target="_blank">implementation (Java)</a>. <a href="https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/python-program-for-stooge-sort/" target="_blank">(Python)</a>.
<h2>More information</h2>
<p>
Stooge sort <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bfzYj-qGw7U" target="_blank">illustrated</a> and stooge sort vs bubble sort. <br /> <iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/bfzYj-qGw7U" frameborder="0" allowfullscreen></iframe> Bogo sort vs. stooge sort <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bfzYj-qGw7U&t=355" target="_blank">race</a>. <br /> <iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/bfzYj-qGw7U?start=355" frameborder="0" allowfullscreen></iframe>
</p>

